1
00:00:02,001 --> 00:00:03,706
Between the seventh and eighth books there's

2
00:00:03,726 --> 00:00:06,481
a short story called Auberon.

3
00:00:06,501 --> 00:00:08,581
Laconia has taken the gates,

4
00:00:08,601 --> 00:00:10,331
and now it has to rule more

5
00:00:10,351 --> 00:00:12,256
than a thousand worlds.

6
00:00:12,276 --> 00:00:13,906
Auberon is one of the richest

7
00:00:13,926 --> 00:00:15,656
of them, and its new governor

8
00:00:15,676 --> 00:00:17,256
is about to learn how hard

9
00:00:17,276 --> 00:00:19,206
that job really is.

10
00:00:19,226 --> 00:00:20,543
Spoilers ahead!

11
00:00:21,278 --> 00:00:23,983
Biryar Rittenaur is a Laconian officer,

12
00:00:24,003 --> 00:00:25,633
and a true believer.

13
00:00:25,653 --> 00:00:27,705
Duarte sends him to govern Auberon,

14
00:00:27,725 --> 00:00:30,388
a busy trading world full of ships,

15
00:00:30,408 --> 00:00:32,093
money, and crime.

16
00:00:32,113 --> 00:00:33,443
He brings his wife Mona,

17
00:00:33,463 --> 00:00:35,188
a soil scientist,

18
00:00:35,208 --> 00:00:36,738
and a simple plan:

19
00:00:36,758 --> 00:00:38,338
clean the place up.

20
00:00:38,358 --> 00:00:40,233
No bribes, no smuggling,

21
00:00:40,253 --> 00:00:42,398
and Laconian law for everyone.

22
00:00:43,048 --> 00:00:45,528
But Auberon already has its own rulers.

23
00:00:45,548 --> 00:00:48,603
A hidden crime boss runs the docks,

24
00:00:48,623 --> 00:00:50,848
the police, and half the government.

25
00:00:50,878 --> 00:00:54,228
He's Erich, Amos's old friend from Baltimore,

26
00:00:54,248 --> 00:00:56,153
the forger who once gave Amos

27
00:00:56,173 --> 00:00:57,428
his new name.

28
00:00:57,448 --> 00:01:00,053
The governor's crackdown goes nowhere.

29
00:01:00,073 --> 00:01:02,123
Erich doesn't fight him head on.

30
00:01:02,148 --> 00:01:03,353
He finds the one thing

31
00:01:03,373 --> 00:01:05,178
the governor can't protect:

32
00:01:05,198 --> 00:01:06,655
the woman he loves.

33
00:01:07,386 --> 00:01:07,891
In the end,

34
00:01:07,911 --> 00:01:09,266
the governor keeps his title,

35
00:01:09,286 --> 00:01:11,861
but he rules on Erich's terms.

36
00:01:11,976 --> 00:01:16,006
Laconia's reports say Auberon is calm and loyal.

37
00:01:16,026 --> 00:01:19,481
Underneath, it runs the way it always has.

38
00:01:19,501 --> 00:01:21,331
Laconia can conquer a world

39
00:01:21,351 --> 00:01:22,306
in a day.

40
00:01:22,326 --> 00:01:24,247
Ruling one is something else.

41
00:01:24,953 --> 00:01:27,853
That is the crack in Laconia's empire.

42
00:01:27,953 --> 00:01:30,263
Its colonies obey on the surface,

43
00:01:30,283 --> 00:01:32,838
and keep their own rules underneath.

44
00:01:32,858 --> 00:01:34,958
Naomi will remember that.

45
00:01:34,983 --> 00:01:36,563
When she needs a place to rebuild

46
00:01:36,583 --> 00:01:39,538
the resistance, she goes to Auberon.

47
00:01:39,558 --> 00:01:42,698
Next up: book eight, Tiamat's Wrath.

